 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "workers lists distinct worker names; tasks lists [id, duration] pairs (distinct ids, positive durations) processed in the given order. A worker's workload is the sum of durations of tasks already given to that worker. Level 2 (inferred): specialties[i] lists the task types worker i can handle and taskTypes[k] is the type of task k. Give each task to the eligible worker (whose specialties contain the task type) with the smallest workload, ties to the lexicographically smallest name; a task with no eligible worker is left unassigned. Return the per-worker id lists in worker order followed by one extra list of unassigned task ids in task order.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk14-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
